alse, or the list is empty and `switch_session` is not offered. A repo's setup script is never for the Default. In any other environment, edit when `editable_by_you` is true, whichever repository it was made for; otherwise propose a personal environment with create_environment, or tell the user the `not_editable_reason`. request_credential saves on the environment this session runs in. (5) Propose once and say why, with the evidence. If the user declines, do not propose a change for that need again in this session.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"environment_id": {"description": "The environment ID to look up (starts with 'env_'), e.g. from list_environments. Omit to look up the environment this session is running in.", "type": "string"}}, "required": [], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__get_environment"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "Fetch a single transcript event from a Claude Code Remote session by session_id and event_uuid. Returns the event's role, content, isSynthetic, and inbound_origin. Same authorization as list_events.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__get_event", "schema": {"description": "Fetch a single transcript event from a Claude Code Remote session by session_id and event_uuid. Returns the event's role, content, isSynthetic, and inbound_origin. Same authorization as list_events.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"event_uuid": {"description": "The event uuid to read.", "type": "string"}, "session_id": {"description": "The session ID that owns the event.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["session_id", "event_uuid"], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__get_event"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "Get details for a specific Claude Code Remote session by ID. Returns the session's title, status, status_bucket (working / blocked / review_ready / completed / failed — 'failed' means its last turn errored), creation 